Subject: [PATCH 11/16] luks2: the Linux LUKS partition type; DriveSetup names
 LUKS2 volumes

DriveSetup listed an encrypted partition as "Unknown (Linux data)": its
list names only file systems it recognises, and wrote the same text into
the Partition type column too.

- The GPT type CA7D7CCB-63ED-4C53-861C-1742536059CC and MBR type 0xe8
  are in Haiku's partition type lists as "Linux LUKS", so DriveSetup
  shows and offers them.
- EncryptedVolume's Encrypt gives the partition that type after
  formatting it, where the partitioning system has it; a failure is
  only logged. A partition typed "Be File System" (DriveSetup's
  default) is then no longer taken for one by a boot loader.
- DriveSetup's list: "LUKS2 encrypted" under File system and the
  header's name under Volume name for a LUKS2 partition or disk (also
  with only the secondary header intact); the Partition type column
  shows the type itself.

GUI test: partition 2 starts as BFS and must end up Linux LUKS (checked
on the host with sgdisk); a DriveSetup screenshot. 4 of 4, the guest
25 of 25, the installed disk 5 of 5.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
